    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-algebra-2007-p4.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathbf{4 3} \\text {. }}{63}\\) Use the factorizations \\(n^{3}-1=(n-1)\\left(n^{2}+n+1\\right)\\) and \\(n^{3}+1=(n+1)\\left(n^{2}-n+1\\right)\\) to write\n\n\\[\\frac{1 \\cdot 7}{3 \\cdot 3} \\cdot \\frac{2 \\cdot 13}{4 \\cdot 7} \\cdot \\frac{3 \\cdot 21}{5 \\cdot 13} \\cdot \\frac{4 \\cdot 31}{6 \\cdot 21} \\cdot \\frac{5 \\cdot 43}{7 \\cdot 31}=\\frac{1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 43}{3 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 7}=\\frac{43}{63}\\]",
